// Secrets.example.xcconfig
// Template — copy this to `Secrets.xcconfig` (which is git-ignored) and fill in
// your real values. NEVER commit Secrets.xcconfig.
//
//     cp Secrets.example.xcconfig Secrets.xcconfig
//
// Wire it up in Xcode: Project ▸ Info ▸ Configurations ▸ set both Debug and
// Release to use `Secrets`. Then surface the values to Info.plist (e.g.
// SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY user-defined keys) so the app can read them.

// ⚠️ xcconfig gotcha: a literal "//" is parsed as a comment, so a URL like
// https://abc.supabase.co would be truncated at "https:". Break it with $() :
SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co

// The PUBLISHABLE (anon) key — safe to ship in a client app; RLS is the real
// guard. Do NOT put the service_role / secret key in the app.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = YOUR-PUBLISHABLE-ANON-KEY
